redfin 1086: call route + gains + DTMF diagnostics (coder V, 2026-11-13). Self-contained; delete this file to drop it.
- kern.sweet_voice_route 0 unset (default) / 1 earpiece / 2 speaker: switches a running call (amplifier only, CVP kept),
  and is the auto trigger's mode for the next call. /dev/redwood-audio ioctl _IOW('r', 2, uint32_t) = the same from
  RedwoodAudio (Receiver/Speaker); used for the auto start only if it came within 15 s before it.
- kern.sweet_voice_gain_rx (dB, default 0): call amplifier level relative to below_ear/below_spk (cap unchanged).
- kern.sweet_voice_gain_tx (dB, default 0): mic ADC gain during calls relative to micgain (sweet_mic.c gain_apply()).
- kern.sweet_voice_dtmflog (default 1, logs only): VOICE DTMF requests/answers/inds, Apple AUDIO (0xe1) request ids,
  "NO ANSWER in 5 s" with the message id.

